{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-13802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{9}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}{ln}^{3}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =6\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+C \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{ln}^{3}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "3{ln}^{3}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "{e}^{3x}+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "{log}_{3}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡(2x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{3}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-210781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\int u\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}){log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{3}^{2}⁡x}{4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-31400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $32$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{u}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $81$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(2-1) \\\\  & =(4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-351283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $125$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-351287" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-351287" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $e/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-13845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot {u}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5"} {"question" "q-346434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "q-346434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{75}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7409707c354b53ff0369608c2246b1bcc66f0c3cbe6249ae6c12ba1ef63d32e"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0"}] "usage" {"q-31401" [] "e-14405" [] "q-13802" [] "e-14406" [] "q-31329" [] "e-14422" []} "basis" 1137 "retractions" [[17592186101057 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $∫(2)/(x\\ln (2x))dx$."] [17592186101287 :question/problem "What is $∫\\frac{\\log_{2} x}{x}dx$?"] [17592186101290 :question/problem "What is $∫(\\log_{3} (x^{2}))/(x)dx$?"] [17592186100521 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186100521 :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\ln x}}dx &= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}du \\\\\n&= 3∫u^{-1/2}du \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2u^{1/2} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{u} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{\\ln x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100522 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x}{x} \\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186100522 :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2}{x} \\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x$. Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫((\\log_{3} x)^{2})/(x)dx &= ∫(\\log_{3} x)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫u^{2} \\cdot \\ln 3du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3∫u^{2}du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}u^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3(\\log_{3} x)^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{3} x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100523 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186100523 :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & e & e^{2} \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x &= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x} \\\\[5pt] &=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{7}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186098113 17592186098114 17592186098115 17592186098116 17592186098117 17592186099339 17592186099340 17592186099341 17592186099342 17592186099343 17592186099347 17592186099348 17592186099349 17592186099350 17592186099351] "immutable_fields" [[17592186098112 :answer-field/correct] [17592186098112 :answer-field/id] [17592186098112 :answer-field/key] [17592186098112 :answer-field/type] [17592186099338 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099338 :answer-field/id] [17592186099338 :answer-field/key] [17592186099338 :answer-field/type] [17592186099346 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099346 :answer-field/id] [17592186099346 :answer-field/key] [17592186099346 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
